{
  "what": "Every superseded generation of canonical rows, by the document each was read at. `byDocumentSha256` is the lookup: a twelve-hex document hash — active or receded — maps to the file holding the rows that name it.",
  "rule": "A file is named by the ACTIVE document's twelve-hex SHA-256. A receded document never names a file; it is a difference over the active document of its own scheme and travels with it. Where only the receded document moved and the active one still ships, the name is the compound `<active>-<receded>`, because the active hash alone would name this file after a generation that is current.",
  "claimsFields": "`readUnderClaims` is the claims section of the gate whose read produced these rows; `movedUnderClaims` is the section of the gate that superseded them and moved them here. They are never the same gate. Split in two on 2026-09-20 (c9a §5.159b §10, finding 8), when one field named `readUnderClaims` was being written with the mover's section by some gates and the reader's by others, and README.md's table disagreed with it.",
